ur.insert(best_pos, farthest_city)\n        in_tour.add(farthest_city)\n    # Simple 2-opt improvement\n    improved = True\n    while improved:\n        improved = False\n        for i in range(n-2):\n            for j in range(i+2, n):\n                a, b, c, d = tour[i], tour[i+1], tour[j], tour[(j+1)%n]\n                if distance_matrix[a, c] + distance_matrix[b, d] < distance_matrix[a, b] + distance_matrix[c, d]:\n                    tour[i+1:j+1] = reversed(tour[i+1:j+1])\n                    improved = True\n                    break\n            if improved:\n                break\n    report_best_tour(np.array(tour))\n    return np.array(tour)\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000003 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Farthest insertion with 2-opt produces valid, timeout-free tours but tour length is moderate for 500-city instances.\n- Aim: Reduce tour length by adding a stronger local search or restart mechanism to escape local optima.\n- Preserve: farthest insertion construction for initial tours; 2-opt improvement loop; report_best_tour usage; deterministic timeout-robust behavior\n- Change: add 3-opt move or double-bridge perturbation to diversify search; optionally restart with different random seeds or shuffled construction\n- Avoid: removing construction heuristic entirely; changes that increase runtime beyond 60s timeout; introducing non-valid permutations\n\nDistance is the search objective for TSP; lower distance is better.\n\nImplement a complete TSP metaheuristic inside this required entrypoint:\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n\nRequirements:\n- Minimize total TSP tour distance.\n- Return a 1D np.ndarray containing each node exactly once.\n- Do not repeat the start node at the end.\n- Always return a valid tour.\n- Use only distance_matrix; do not assume coord